course: dictionary
lesson: 2283
title: A word for dawn and dusk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are hard because they name one exact thing. «Crepuscular» is one of them. Look at the context: «Night animals sleep by day in burrows, tree holes and dark corners, guided by their body clock; animals most active at dawn and dusk, like rabbits and deer, are called crepuscular.» The sentence first describes two groups, night animals and animals active at dawn and dusk, then gives the name of the second group.
explain: Dawn is when the day begins and the sun comes up. Dusk is when the day ends and the sun goes down. So crepuscular must mean active at dawn and dusk. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The word can also describe light. «The crepuscular light» means dim, half-dark light, like the sky at twilight, the time between day and night. The words around it tell you which meaning is right: animals point to the first meaning, and light points to the second.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Crepuscular» means active mainly at dawn and dusk, rather than in the day or night.
fact: In science, animals are grouped by when they are active: day animals, night animals and crepuscular animals.
fact: «Rabbits and deer» are examples of crepuscular animals.
fact: «Crepuscular light» means dim, half-dark light, like twilight.
exercise: «Rabbits and deer are most active at dawn and dusk, so they are called crepuscular.» What does crepuscular mean? | *Active mainly at dawn and dusk | Asleep all day in a burrow | Glowing in the dark | Active only at midday
exercise: Lily sees «crepuscular rays» through the clouds at sunset. What are they? | Lightning flashing across the sky | Stars shining in the night sky | *Beams of sunlight shining through gaps in clouds | Rain falling from dark clouds
exercise: «The crepuscular light made the field look grey and dim.» What does crepuscular mean here? | Very loud | Bright and sunny | Cold and wet | *Dim and half-dark, like twilight
test: Which is the best meaning of crepuscular? | Active mainly in the day | *Active mainly at twilight, at dawn and dusk | Made of glass | Active only at midnight
test: A deer is a crepuscular animal. When is it most active? | In the middle of the night | *At dawn and dusk | Only when it rains | Midday
exam: «Night animals sleep by day in burrows, tree holes and dark corners.» Which word in the example sentence names the animals that are active at dawn and dusk? | Night | Burrows | *Crepuscular | Corners
